<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xml:id="KR3a0047" type="notes"><teiHeader><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Research Notes for 朱子語類</title><editor role="creator">TLS Project</editor></titleStmt><publicationStmt><p>published electronically as part of the TLS project at https://hxwd.org</p><availability status="2">This work has been licensed for use in the TLS</availability></publicationStmt><sourceDesc><bibl><title>Research Notes</title></bibl><p>Comments and notes to <bibl corresp="#KR3a0047"><title xml:lang="och">朱子語類</title></bibl>.</p></sourceDesc></fileDesc><profileDesc><creation resp="#Anna.Wand">Initially created: <date>2022-03-15T23:50:54.362+09:00</date> by Anna.Wand</creation></profileDesc></teiHeader><text><body><div><head>Comments</head><p xml:id="KR3a0047-start"><seg corresp="#KR3a0047_tls_137-60a.16" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-09-01T22:10:02.596+09:00">Li Ao of Tang times himself maintained in an essay that Wang Tong could be compared to the Tai Gong family,</seg><seg corresp="#KR3a0047_tls_137-60a.17" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-09-01T22:23:01.227+09:00">so his books have already been around for a long time. </seg><seg corresp="#KR3a0047_tls_137-60a.18" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-09-01T22:26:16.418+09:00">Yi Chuan considered that Master Wenzhong had some bon mots</seg><seg corresp="#KR3a0047_tls_137-60a.19" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-09-01T22:27:09.895+09:00">but they got polluted by later additions.</seg><seg corresp="#KR3a0047_tls_137-60a.20" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-09-01T22:31:04.33+09:00">By the looks of it, they must have been blown up by the crew around Ruan </seg><seg corresp="#KR3a0047_tls_137-63a.7" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-09-01T22:44:24.038+09:00">The present annotations</seg><seg corresp="#KR3a0047_tls_137-63a.8" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-09-01T22:45:01.297+09:00">are basically Ruan Yi's commentaries;</seg><seg corresp="#KR3a0047_tls_137-63a.9" generatedBy="human" xml:lang="en" resp="#CH" modified="2026-09-01T23:20:18.728+09:00">Gong Dingchen there is an edition with commentaries</seg></p></div></body></text></TEI>